From: Husk Rebuilt contributors
Subject: [PATCH] configure: mark iOS cross executables as requiring a wrapper
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Husk's iOS build targets Darwin arm64, which matches Apple Silicon macOS in
Meson's system/cpu checks without sharing its executable platform. QEMU emits
its own config-meson.cross rather than inheriting Husk's dependency cross file.
Tell Meson not to execute iOS compiler sanity probes on the macOS build host.
This patch is applied only by Husk's iOS build script.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1843,6 +1843,7 @@ if test "$skip_meson" = no; then
 
   echo "# Automatically generated by configure - do not modify" > $cross
   echo "[properties]" >> $cross
+  echo "needs_exe_wrapper = true" >> $cross
 
   # unroll any custom device configs
   for a in $device_archs; do
